   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Talking about what you eat",
     "texto": [
      "Liker means «to like»: Jeg liker ost means «I like cheese». Unlike Spanish «me gusta», Norwegian uses liker with the person first, as in English. To make it negative, ikke goes after the verb: Jeg liker ikke fisk («I don't like fish»).",
      "Drikker means «I drink» or «you drink»; like other present-tense verbs, it does not change with jeg and du. Eller means «or» when you choose between options."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
